era:LinearElementSection era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LinearElementSectionShape>;
                         a owl:Class;
                         rdfs:comment "Represents a section of a linear element."@en;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy era:;
                         rdfs:label "Linear Element Section"@en;
                         rdfs:subClassOf era:LinearElement;
                         skos:scopeNote "A linear element section is a finer granularity of a linear element, representing a specific portion of it. This concept is introduced to address the cases when a linear element needs to be split such as a part of it is used by a net referencing (more in the paragraph describing the positioning on the network). By using start and end offsets measured from origin of the element in ascending order, sections eliminate the need for intrinsic coordinates and instead rely on distances along the linear element."@en.
era:LinearPositioningSystem era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LinearPositioningSystemShape>;
                            dcterms:created "2024-11-29"^^xsd:date;
                            dcterms:modified "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date;
                            dcterms:replaces era:LineReference;
                            a owl:Class;
                            rdfs:comment """Represents a linear positioning system used for referencing positions on the network.
It can also represent a sequence of one or more sections of line, used for regular railway operations."""@en;
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy era:;
                            rdfs:label "Linear Positioning System"@en;
                            owl:disjointWith era:LinearPositioningSystemCoordinate.
era:LinearPositioningSystemCoordinate era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LinearPositioningSystemCoordinateShape>;
                                      dcterms:created "2024-11-29"^^xsd:date;
                                      a owl:Class;
                                      rdfs:comment "Represents coordinates in a linear positioning system."@en;
