era:etcsNationalPacket44Function era:applicable "Y/N/NYA";
                                 era:dependencyNote "A value has to be provided when ETCS is present (a value is provided on 1.1.1.3.2.1)."@en;
                                 era:inSkosConceptScheme <http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/etcs-national-packet-44-functions/ETCSNationalPacket44Functions>;
                                 era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/EtcsNationalPacket44Function>,
                                                              <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/EtcsNationalPacket44FunctionSKOS>;
                                 dcterms:created "2024-11-20"^^xsd:date;
                                 dcterms:modified "2025-05-05"^^xsd:date,
                                                  "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date,
                                                  "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date;
                                 dcterms:relation era:etcsLevelType;
                                 dcterms:replaces era:etcsNationalPacket44;
                                 dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj>;
                                 a owl:ObjectProperty;
                                 rdfs:comment "Indication whether data for national applications is transmitted between track and train."@en;
                                 rdfs:domain [a owl:Class ; 
                                              owl:unionOf ()];
                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy era:;
                                 rdfs:label "ETCS national packet 44 application implemented"@en;
                                 rdfs:range skos:Concept;
                                 rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.era.europa.eu/domains/technical-specifications-interoperability/control-command-and-signalling-tsi_en#oe-content-paragraph-1632"^^xsd:anyURI;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf era:tsiCompliantTrainProtectionSystemObjParameter;
                                 status:term_status "stable";
                                 skos:scopeNote """Value can be `false` or a link to the implemented functions.

Packets 44 are the means to transmit data for national applications between train and track and vice versa, using the data transmission facilities included within the ETCS. 
NID_XUSER values managed by ERA in a document about ETCS variables available on ERA website. 

See: TSI CCS (7.4.3 & 6.2.4.2)"""@en.
